This is a hybrid, new and existing business, end-to-end sales role within our growing Sportsbook customer vertical.&nbsp; Genius is the leading provider of sophisticated data-driven software to regulated sportsbook operators around the globe - providing them with everything they need to manage their operation and grow profits.&nbsp; Our multi-award-winning technology is built to help our partners maximise their performance through live sports data, engaging betting content, and outsourced sportsbook management services. We’re the trusted partner to over 250 sportsbook brands including Sky Bet, bet365, William Hill and more. &nbsp;

In this dynamic role, the successful candidate will immerse themselves in the sports betting industry to understand the complex technological and regulatory developments facing the industry and how Genius’ software and trading products can add value in meeting customer needs.&nbsp; You will use a consultative approach to discover and understand client requirements, match Genius products and services to those requirements, and unlock new opportunities for mutual value creation. &nbsp;

The ideal candidate will bring a track record of consistently achieving challenging targets, a strong personal drive to over-achieve, and be a natural self-starter who can find and deliver business from both new and existing customers without the need to be tightly managed. &nbsp;

Key Responsibilities &nbsp;

• Managing the entire end-to-end sales process with new Sportsbook prospects, from lead generation to contract closure &nbsp;

• Responsible for all commercial strategy and execution across a book of existing customers within EMEA, including all renewal and upsell sales processes &nbsp;

• Develop and manage a strong pipeline of opportunities, ensuring accurate forecasting and consistent progression through the sales cycle &nbsp;

• Work closely with product teams to position sportsbook solutions tailored to client needs &nbsp;

• Build and maintain strategic relationships with key stakeholders across the sports betting ecosystem &nbsp;

• Establishing new, collaborative relationships with leaders across the global sales team &nbsp;

• Identify and evaluate new market opportunities (regulated and emerging markets), including understanding local betting regulations and competitive landscapes &nbsp;

• Stay up to date with sportsbook trends, customer behavior, and regulatory changes to inform sales strategy and identify new opportunities &nbsp;

• Represent the business at industry events, conferences, and client meetings to strengthen market presence and generate leads &nbsp;

• Demonstrate strong operational hygiene including following internal sales processes and updating CRM systems and other documentation in a timely manner &nbsp;

